    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reacting: à, thế à, chắc, nhỉ, chúc mừng",
     "texto": [
      "These little words make you sound natural, not like a textbook:",
      "**…à?** at the end shows interest or concern. Someone says «Tôi mệt lắm» and you say: **Cô mệt lắm à?** = Are you very tired? (in English it might sound like doubt; in Vietnamese it's caring).",
      "**Thế à?** = Oh, really? / Really?",
      "**chắc / chắc là** = surely, must be: **Chắc là ông mệt lắm.** = You must be very tired.",
      "**…nhỉ** at the end: «right?, don't you think?». It looks for the other person to agree: **Đẹp quá nhỉ!** = How pretty, right?",
      "**Chúc mừng!** = Congratulations! · **Tôi mừng cho bà.** = I'm happy for you, madam."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
